From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00
Subject: [PATCH] QCocoaTheme: create the role palette colors lazily

The table of role palette text colors was a namespace-scope array whose
initializer calls +[NSColor controlTextColor] and three similar class
methods, so it ran as a static initializer of every executable that links
the cocoa plugin statically, before main(), even in a process that never
creates the theme or a window. Initializing the dynamic system colors
there connects the process to the window server, the render server,
LaunchServices, tccd and distnoted, and reads preferences. A process that
restricts itself with a sandbox profile later cannot drop those
connections.

Build the table in qt_mac_createRolePalettes(), its only user, which runs
when the theme first builds its role palettes. The colors are dynamic and
are resolved when converted, under the same drawing appearance as before,
so the palettes stay the same.

Origin: desktop-app; based on Qt 6.11.2.
---

diff --git a/src/plugins/platforms/cocoa/qcocoatheme.mm b/src/plugins/platforms/cocoa/qcocoatheme.mm
index a5d45ef..7b61cc0 100644
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/cocoa/qcocoatheme.mm
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/cocoa/qcocoatheme.mm
@@ -113,29 +113,29 @@ inline QMacPaletteMap(QPlatformTheme::Palette p, NSColor *a, NSColor *i) :
     QPlatformTheme::Palette paletteRole;
 };
 
+static QHash<QPlatformTheme::Palette, QPalette*> qt_mac_createRolePalettes()
+{
 #define MAC_PALETTE_ENTRY(pal, active, inactive) \
     QMacPaletteMap(pal, [NSColor active], [NSColor inactive])
-static QMacPaletteMap mac_widget_colors[] = {
